n Conflict. 1st Fleet is based in Gudgorga. \r\n\r\nRegiment composition in 1332 NE:\r\n— fleet: 2."},{"id":"regiment13-4","name":"2nd Fleet","legend":"Regiment was formed in 1329 Newbury Era during the Swampian Conflict. 2nd Fleet is based in Kegkabaram. \r\n\r\nRegiment composition in 1332 NE:\r\n— fleet: 1."},{"id":"regiment14-0","name":"1st (Bilgab) Regiment","legend":"Regiment was formed in 1328 Newbury Era during the Hlamben Expedition. 1st (Bilgab) Regiment is stationed in Bilgab. \r\n\r\nRegiment composition in 1332 NE:\r\n— archers: 1466\r\n— cavalry: 163\r\n— artillery: 31\r\n— infantry: 1342."},{"id":"regiment14-1","name":"2nd (Gundin) Regiment","legend":"Regiment was formed in 1331 Newbury Era during the Bundus War. 2nd (Gundin) Regiment is stationed in Gunzar. \r\n\r\nRegiment composition in 1332 NE:\r\n— archers: 658\r\n— artillery: 4\r\n— cavalry: 47\r\n— infantry: 531."},{"id":"marker0","name":"Mount Midford","legend":"Dormant volcano. Height: 3721m."},{"id":"marker1","name":"Hot Springs of Melion","legend":"A geothermal springs with naturally heated water that provide relaxation and medicinal benefits. Average temperature is 20°C."},{"id":"marker2","name":"Rrharquelwen Healing Spring","legend":"This legendary water source is whispered about in ancient tales and believed to possess mystical properties. The spring emanates crystal-clear water, shimmering with an otherworldly iridescence that sparkles even in the dimmest light."},{"id":"marker3","name":"Qhazri — iron mining town","legend":"Qhazri is a mining town of 10491 people just nearby the iron mine."},{"id":"marker4","name":"Unul — salt mining town","legend":"Unul is a mining town of 3057 people just nearby the salt mine."},{"id":"marker5","name":"Whilent — salt mining town","legend":"Whilent is a mining town of 3003 people just nearby the salt mine."},{"id":"marker6","name":"Asadrin — silver mining town","legend":"Asadrin is a mining town of 1562 people just nearby the silver mine."},{"id":"marker7","name":"Mornkuc — salt mining town","legend":"Mornkuc is a mining town of 8824 people just nearby the salt mine."},{"id":"marker8","name":"Yoltunse — silver mining town","legend":"Yoltunse is a mining town of 5841 people just nearby the silver mine."},{"id":"marker9","name":"Scorchpost — salt mining town","legend":"Scorchpost is a mining town of 2374 people just nearby the salt mine."},{"id":"marker10","name":"Guzan — salt mining town","legend":"Guzan is a mining town of 6483 people just nearby the salt mine."},{"id":"marker11","name":"Baykale Bridge","legend":"A rickety bridge spans over the Aynak River near Baykale."},{"id":"marker12","name":"Tengrilya Bridge","legend":"A formidable bridge spans over the Bale River near Tengrilya."},{"id":"marker13","name":"Tekekev Bridge","legend":"A rickety bridge spans over the Beykutlu River near Tekekev."},{"id":"marker14","name":"The Pink Badger","legend":"A big and famous roadside tavern. Delicious cured badger with sparkling rom is served here."},{"id":"marker15","name":"The Brave Antelope","legend":"A big and famous roadside inn. Delicious syrupped turkey with misty cider is served here."},{"id":"marker16","name":"The Hungry Tavern","legend":"A big and famous roadside tavern. Delicious pickled pears with black mead is served here."},{"id":"marker17","name":"The Happy Tavern","legend":"A big and famous roadside tavern. Delicious steamed catfish with green milk is served here."},{"id":"marker18","name":"The Loud Shark","legend":"A big and famous roadside tavern. Delicious dressed shark with red brandy is served here."},{"id":"marker19","name":"The Green Badger","legend":"A big and famous roadside tavern. Delicious poached pumpkin with salty gin is served here."},{"id":"marker20","name":"The Blue Eagle","legend":"A big and famous roadside tavern. Delicious dry-aged eagle with ice wine is served here."},{"id":"marker21","name":"The Red Jaguar","legend":"A big and famous roadside tavern. Delicious dry-aged beet with red kvass is served here."},{"id":"marker22","name":"Ginerean Lighthouse","legend":"A lighthouse to serve as a beacon for ships in the open sea."},{"id":"marker23","name":"Felsearian Lighthouse","legend":"A lighthouse to serve as a beacon for ships in the open sea."},{"id":"marker24","name":"Gabad Waterfall","legend":"A breathtaking waterfall cuts through the landscape."},{"id":"marker25","name":"Wildermide Battlefield","legend":"A historical battle of the Emberglenese Campaign. \r\nDate: November 11, 1139 Newbury Era."},{"id":"marker26","name":"Dragon Battlefield","legend":"A historical battle of the Sivyurt War. \r\nDate: April 9, 1155 Newbury Era."},{"id":"marker27","name":"Shagoon Battlefield","legend":"A historical battle of the Khathugan War. \r\nDate: February 4, 1274 Newbury Era."},{"id":"marker28","name":"Dungeon","legend":"<div>Undiscovered dungeon. See <a href=\"https://watabou.github.io/one-page-dungeon/?seed=207144807296\" target=\"_blank\">One page dungeon</a></div><iframe style=\"pointer-events: none;\" src=\"https://watabou.github.io/one-page-dungeon/?seed=207144807296\" sandbox=\"allow-scripts allow-same-origin\"></iframe>"},{"id":"marker29","name":"Dungeon","legend":"<div>Undiscovered dungeon. See <a href=\"https://watabou.github.io/one-page-dungeon/?seed=207144807617\" target=\"_blank\">One page dungeon</a></div><iframe style=\"pointer-events: none;\" src=\"https://watabou.github.io/one-page-dungeon/?seed=207144807617\" sandbox=\"allow-scripts allow-same-origin\"></iframe>"},{"id":"marker30","name":"Dungeon","legend":"<div>Undiscovered dungeon. See <a href=\"https://watabou.github.io/one-page-dungeon/?seed=2071448073185\" target=\"_blank\">One page dungeon</a></div><iframe style=\"pointer-events: none;\" src=\"https://watabou.github.io/one-page-dungeon/?seed=2071448073185\" sandbox=\"allow-scripts allow-same-origin\"></iframe>"},{"id":"marker31","name":"Dungeon","legend":"<div>Undiscovered dungeon. See <a href=\"https://watabou.github.io/one-page-dungeon/?seed=2071448071166\" target=\"_blank\">One page dungeon</a></div><iframe style=\"pointer-events: none;\" src=\"https://watabou.github.io/one-page-dungeon/?seed=2071448071166\" sandbox=\"allow-scripts allow-same-origin\"></iframe>"},{"id":"marker32","name":"Cragcoast Monster","legend":"Journeying folk say a relic monster of 7 m long inhabits Cragcoast Lake. Truth or lie, folks are afraid to fish in the lake."},{"id":"marker33","name":"Witon Monster","legend":"Old sailors tell stories of a gigantic sea monster inhabiting these dangerous waters. Rumors say it can be 10 m long."},{"id":"marker34","name":"Swampmoor Bearded Devil","legend":"Locals speak of a superior Bearded Devil who inhabits Swampmoor hills and harasses travelers in the area."},{"id":"marker35","name":"Houndpass Cyclops","legend":"Legends speak of a feared Cyclops who inhabits Houndpass hills and steals cattle at night."},{"id":"marker36","name":"Ulmtoilm Forest","legend":"A forest sacred to local Kobold (Goblin) Forefathers."},{"id":"marker37","name":"Utiarm Forest","legend":"A forest sacred to local Kobold (Goblin) Forefathers."},{"id":"marker38","name":"Yithu Pinery","legend":"A pinery sacred to local Arago (Arachnid)ism."},{"id":"marker39","name":"Elunyuetheas Palm Grove","legend":"A palm grove sacred to local Eldar (Elfish) Beliefs."},{"id":"marker40","name":"Mosswind Jaguars","legend":"A gang of forest brigands."},{"id":"marker41","name":"Givzienis Boars","legend":"A gang of forest bandits."},{"id":"marker42","name":"Goladrinn Badgers","legend":"A gang of forest bandits."},{"id":"marker43","name":"Pirates","legend":"Pirate ships have been spotted in these waters."},{"id":"marker44","name":"Pirates","legend":"Pirate ships have been spotted in these waters."},{"id":"marker45","name":"Gob Column","legend":"An ancient column. It has an inscription, but no one can translate it:\n        <div style=\"font-size: 1.8em; line-break: anywhere;\"> ለበበፀሀዐበጠ  ከነአከፀሐፈሰፀበኀወጸዐኀጠኀ ኀ ጸኀየ ከዘረረወወዘዐ ደሠፐዐ</div>"},{"id":"marker46","name":"Snowbay Effigy","legend":"An ancient effigy. It has an inscription, but no one can translate it:\n        <div style=\"font-size: 1.8em; line-break: anywhere;\">༺༽༬༒༅༇༈༆༉༨༘༙༘༈༛༂༜༂༇༚ༀ༡༅ༀ༷༈༕༵༸༙༛༒༱༬༄༦༈ༀ༿༿༫༺༊༔༇༥༴༅༄༅༪༗༤༄༷༂༊༬༊༿༽༾༸༘༥༙༬༢༠༫༓༑༐༣༉༰༒༺༇༚༂༯</div>"},{"id":"marker47","name":"Ruined Castle","legend":"Ruins of an ancient castle. Untold riches may lie within."},{"id":"marker48","name":"Ruined Town","legend":"Ruins of an ancient town. Untold riches may lie within."},{"id":"marker49","name":"Ruined Outpost","legend":"Ruins of an ancient outpost. Untold riches may lie within."},{"id":"marker50","name":"Albeyale Archive","legend":"A vast collection of knowledge, including many rare and ancient tomes."},{"id":"marker51","name":"Travelling Extraordinary Circus","legend":"Roll up, roll up, this extraordinary circus is here for a limited time only."},{"id":"marker52","name":"Travelling Extraordinary Circus","legend":"Roll up, roll up, this extraordinary circus is here for a limited time only."},{"id":"marker53","name":"Asadrauth Contest","legend":"Warriors from around the land gather for a contest of the greats in Asadrauth, with fame, fortune and favour on offer to the victor."},{"id":"marker54","name":"Kleab Fair","legend":"A fair is being held in Kleab, with all manner of local and foreign goods and services on offer."},{"id":"marker55","name":"Minor Jetty","legend":"A small location along the Dilent River to launch boats from sits here, along with a weary looking owner, willing to sell passage along the river."},{"id":"marker56","name":"Jaguars migration","legend":"A huge group of jaguars are migrating, whether part of their annual routine, or something more extraordinary."},{"id":"marker57","name":"Vreaxair Ravine","legend":"The Vreaxair Ravine. Locals claim that it is the home of strange monsters."},{"id":"marker58","name":"Dograven Portal","legend":"An element of the magic portal system connecting major city. The portals were installed centuries ago, but still work fine."},{"id":"marker59","name":"Bilgab Portal","legend":"An element of the magic portal system connecting major city. The portals were installed centuries ago, but still work fine."},{"id":"marker60","name":"Shake Portal","legend":"An element of the magic portal system connecting major city. The portals were installed centuries ago, but still work fine."},{"id":"marker61","name":"Baraled Portal","legend":"An element of the magic portal system connecting major city. The portals were installed centuries ago, but still work fine."},{"id":"marker62","name":"Alpseri Portal","legend":"An element of the magic portal system connecting major city. The portals were installed centuries ago, but still work fine."},{"id":"marker63","name":"Bozde Portal","legend":"An element of the magic portal system connecting major city. The portals were installed centuries ago, but still work fine."},{"id":"marker64","name":"Blix Portal","legend":"An element of the magic portal system connecting major city. The portals were installed centuries ago, but still work fine."},{"id":"marker65","name":"Iahzit Portal","legend":"An element of the magic portal system connecting major city. The portals were installed centuries ago, but still work fine."},{"id":"marker66","name":"Demonic Rift","legend":"A rumoured demonic rift in this area is causing swarms of foes to spill forth."},{"id":"marker67","name":"Disturbed Burial","legend":"A burial site has been disturbed in this area, causing the dead to rise and attack the living."},{"id":"marker68","name":"Ashton Tomb","legend":"A labyrinthine necropolis where each step echoes with haunting murmurs. The walls are adorned with ancient runes, and restless spirits guide or hinder those who dare to delve into its depths."},{"id":"marker69","name":"Random encounter","legend":"<div>You have encountered a character.</div><iframe src=\"https://deorum.vercel.app/encounter/1765\" width=\"375\" height=\"600\" sandbox=\"allow-scripts allow-same-o